# FIXED DEFECT 2128, 2026-10-18, lane lane-readonly-lend (M-readonly-lend
# step 7; panel 224's R4 filed it apart).
#
# SYMPTOM: `K_NONE`, a name the header never defines, was told alone at
# exit 1, and `K_DIV`, which only the probe sees, on the next build.
#
# CAUSE: the probe was asked only once every unit had compiled, and clang
# refuses this unit at `K_NONE`'s accessor, its assertions and its `return`.
#
# FIX: the unit asked again with `K_NONE`'s accessor written inert, every
# error clang reported standing in it (`cli/value_beside.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2128-values.h"
    constant K_NONE: i64  #~ ffi_unknown_name
    constant K_DIV: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type

function main()
    print(K_NONE + K_DIV)
